<p>
  Walk-in showers are the most-requested bathroom upgrade in Plano — especially in master baths where the garden tub goes unused. A custom walk-in shower is almost always part of a full bathroom remodel, and understanding what drives its cost helps you budget realistically.
</p>

<h2>What a walk-in shower costs</h2>
<p>
  A custom walk-in shower is typically included in a full bathroom remodel, which runs <strong>$20,000–$40,000</strong> for most Plano bathrooms, with high-end master baths reaching up to <strong>$75,000</strong>. Within that, the shower is usually the largest single feature. The biggest cost drivers:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Size and shape</strong> — a curbless, open-concept shower on the same footprint as the old tub is the most common and most cost-effective approach.</li>
  <li><strong>Tile</strong> — large-format porcelain is the value leader; natural stone and premium tile sit at the top of the range.</li>
  <li><strong>Glass</strong> — frameless glass panels and enclosures add cost but open up the space and show off the tile.</li>
  <li><strong>Plumbing</strong> — keeping the shower on the existing drain and supply lines keeps cost down; moving plumbing across the room adds cost and typically a permit.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Garden tub conversions</h2>
<p>
  For Plano homes with an underused garden tub, converting it to a walk-in shower on the same footprint is usually the smartest move — plumbing stays put, so the project is faster and more affordable than a full rework. See our complete guide to <a href="/blog/garden-tub-to-walk-in-shower-plano/">garden tub to walk-in shower conversions in Plano</a>.
</p>

<h2>Design ideas for Plano bathrooms</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Zero-threshold entry</strong> — a barrier-free shower that is easier to use and makes the room feel larger.</li>
  <li><strong>Built-in niches and benches</strong> — soap storage and seating built into the tile, using space the tub once wasted.</li>
  <li><strong>Rain or wall-mount shower heads</strong> — a full fixture upgrade is one of the most popular finishing touches.</li>
  <li><strong>Heated floors</strong> — a favorite in Plano for the cool winter months.</li>
</ul>

